{'symbol': 'DAL', 'date': '2020-07-14 09:30:00', 'title': 'Delta Air Lines Reports Q2 Loss Of $9.01 Per Share', 'text': "QUARTERLY LOSS PER SHARE $9.01.QUARTERLY TOTAL OPERATING REVENUE $1.47 BILLION, DOWN 88%.QUARTERLY ADJUSTED LOSS PER SHARE $4.43.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $-4.07, REVENUE VIEW $1.42 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.JUNE QUARTER CONSOLIDATED UNIT COST (CASM) 59.30 CENTS VERSUS 14.51 CENTS.JUNE QUARTER TRASM DOWN 21%.JUNE QUARTER CASM-EX 41.96 CENTS VERSUS 10.47 CENTS; JUNE QUARTER TRASM, ADJUSTED, DOWN 36%.ENDED JUNE QUARTER WITH $15.7 BILLION IN LIQUIDITY.QUARTERLY TOTAL ADJUSTED REVENUE OF $1.2 BILLION, WHICH EXCLUDES REFINERY SALES, DECLINED 91% ON SYSTEM CAPACITY REDUCTION OF 85%.QUARTERLY ADJUSTED. PRE-TAX LOSS OF $3.9 BILLION EXCLUDES $3.2 BILLION OF ITEMS DIRECTLY RELATED TO IMPACT OFCOVID-19 AND CO'S RESPONSE.AMENDING CREDIT FACILITIES TO REPLACE ALL FIXED CHARGE COVERAGE RATIO COVENANTS WITH LIQUIDITY-BASED COVENANTS.QUARTERLY PASSENGER REVENUES DOWN 94% ON 85% LOWER CAPACITY.QUARTERLY NON-TICKET REVENUE DOWN 65%.DEMAND FOR AIR TRAVEL DECLINED SIGNIFICANTLY IN Q2 AS A RESULT OF COVID-19, WITH ENPLANED PASSENGERS DOWN 93%.EXPECT TO ACHIEVE ADJUSTED COST BASE REDUCTION OF 50% IN SEPT QUARTER.AT END OF JUNE QUARTER, HAD TOTAL DEBT & FINANCING LEASE OBLIGATIONS OF $24.6 BILLION WITH ADJUSTED. NET DEBT OF $13.9 BILLION.IN Q2, RECORDED WRITE-DOWN OF $1.1 BILLION IN INVESTMENT IN LATAM AIRLINES AND $770 MILLION WRITE-DOWN IN INVESTMENT IN AEROMEXICO.WROTE DOWN INVESTMENT IN VIRGIN ATLANTIC IN Q2, RESULTING IN $200 MILLION CHARGE."}
